---
title: "hot_potato_vector lifecycle (Pyth Sui Contracts)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_new: new(vec) [friend only]
    q_new --> q_active: HotPotatoVector { contents: vec }
    q_active --> q_borrow: borrow(potato, i) [friend only]
    q_active --> q_pop: pop_back(potato) [friend only]
    q_active --> q_destroy: destroy(potato) [public]
    q_borrow --> q_active: return reference to element
    q_pop --> q_active: return (elem, potato)
    q_destroy --> [*]: contents dropped

    note right of q_active
        INV-001: HotPotatoVector has no key/store/drop ability
        INV-002: must be consumed (destroyed) within same transaction
        INV-003: only friend modules (pyth::pyth) can create or mutate
        INV-004: enforces that price updates are used before transaction ends
    end note
